{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/12 SAST
Version: 0.7
Description:
  The home page course showcase: nine courses that change every fifteen seconds.

  Server-rendered first, like every other surface. The nine courses in this markup arrive with the
  page, so a reader with no JavaScript sees a full showcase - it simply does not move. Where htmx is
  available the region asks for itself again every fifteen seconds and swaps only itself.

  The next window is carried in this markup rather than counted in the browser: the address this
  region polls already names the cycle after the one being shown, so the server decides what comes
  next and the client only has to ask. That also means a swapped-in region continues the sequence
  instead of restarting it, because it brings its own next address with it.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no comment delimiters and no code, not even to document one.
Changelog:
  2026/09/12 SAST
  - Created for the nine-course rotating showcase.
#}
<div id="course-showcase"
     class="grid grid-3 section"
     hx-get="/courses/showcase?cycle={{ showcase_cycle }}"
     hx-trigger="every 15s"
     hx-target="this"
     hx-swap="outerHTML"
     aria-live="polite">
	{% for course in showcase_courses %}
		{% include '@platform/partials/course-card.html.twig' %}
	{% endfor %}
</div>
